WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:43.405
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:43.675 --> 00:46.695
[Yangju Korea Hospital]

3
00:49.362 --> 00:51.173
Ma'am! Can you hear me?

4
00:51.173 --> 00:53.063
Ma'am! Keep pressure on the wound!

5
00:53.063 --> 00:54.935
Get the red blood cell ready, and set the blood line to max!

6
00:54.935 --> 00:56.733
- Ha Na... - Keep pressing!

7
00:56.733 --> 00:58.433
Ha Na.

8
00:59.909 --> 01:01.396
No, you can't come in!

9
01:01.396 --> 01:02.780
I'm sorry, sir!

10
01:02.780 --> 01:04.985
I'm so sorry, but you can't come in!

11
01:18.225 --> 01:21.476
The suspect weaved through the security camera's blind spots,

12
01:21.476 --> 01:23.813
so he must've done his research on the exit route.

13
01:23.813 --> 01:28.184
We've got the Coast Guard searching the ports for any stowaways,

14
01:28.184 --> 01:32.990
but this seems to have been premeditated.

15
01:37.832 --> 01:39.669
We're past the immediate crisis,

16
01:39.669 --> 01:42.446
but she has suffered great blood loss, and severe brain damage.

17
01:42.446 --> 01:47.416
We'll have to see if she regains consciousness and all organ function.

18
02:00.434 --> 02:02.593
What do we do?

19
02:27.232 --> 02:28.656
What's this?

20
02:28.656 --> 02:32.045
Why do you have this, Woo Jae?

21
02:35.125 --> 02:38.205
I thought you gave it over to Yang Jun Mo.

22
02:41.063 --> 02:44.308
Of course I wouldn't hand over the real one to Yang Jun Mo.

23
02:46.287 --> 02:48.657
You never know what he'd do with it.

24
02:48.657 --> 02:50.951
I kept the real one.

25
02:59.083 --> 03:03.304
Ha Na may not ever regain consciousness,

26
03:03.304 --> 03:07.815
and even if she does, the chance of a full recovery is...

27
03:07.815 --> 03:09.515
small.

28
03:14.190 --> 03:16.029
We've got to find a way.

29
03:16.029 --> 03:17.729
Whatever it takes.

30
03:23.403 --> 03:26.363
It's in smithereens. This is beyond repair.

31
03:26.363 --> 03:28.080
Is there nothing you can do?

32
03:28.080 --> 03:30.424
This is a very old model, you see.

33
03:30.424 --> 03:32.614
I can't get the parts for it.

34
03:33.223 --> 03:35.858
I don't think I can fix this. Here.

35
03:39.815 --> 03:42.659
It's hard to find parts for this model nowadays.

36
03:42.659 --> 03:44.888
We can't fix it, sorry.

37
03:44.888 --> 03:46.288
This can't be fixed.

38
03:46.288 --> 03:47.505
What a relic.

39
03:47.505 --> 03:48.630
No way, nope.

40
03:48.630 --> 03:49.779
This won't do.

41
03:49.779 --> 03:52.075
It's just too old.

42
04:08.496 --> 04:10.150
For me,

43
04:10.150 --> 04:13.723
the fact that I can love you with everything I have...

44
04:13.723 --> 04:16.100
just gives me so much joy.

45
04:16.100 --> 04:18.031
It makes me happy.

46
04:18.031 --> 04:19.731
Woo Jae.

47
04:20.456 --> 04:22.156
I love you.

48
04:24.323 --> 04:26.957
Is the magic gone now?

49
04:28.743 --> 04:30.307
Why can't I...

50
04:30.916 --> 04:33.279
save you?

51
04:36.630 --> 04:39.196
It should've been me, not you.

52
04:40.910 --> 04:43.311
I should've been the one to save you.

53
05:12.856 --> 05:14.769
[Episode 12]

54
05:19.376 --> 05:21.483
What do we do?

55
05:22.843 --> 05:24.908
Is there nothing else we can do?

56
05:25.583 --> 05:27.968
Let's ask around a bit more.

57
05:32.316 --> 05:33.476
Hey.

58
05:33.476 --> 05:34.888
Give it here.

59
05:41.683 --> 05:43.320
Who are you?

60
05:43.320 --> 05:46.423
What's your business?

61
05:48.303 --> 05:50.443
[We Buy, Sell &amp; Repair]

62
05:57.863 --> 05:59.653
Hey, is there any chance...

63
05:59.653 --> 06:02.391
we've met each other somewhere before?

64
06:02.391 --> 06:04.115
I feel like I could recognize you.

65
06:04.115 --> 06:05.457
You think?

66
06:06.083 --> 06:08.885
I don't know. Maybe we passed each other by.

67
06:09.630 --> 06:11.647
- Okay... - This thing...

68
06:11.647 --> 06:13.917
It's on its last life.

69
06:13.917 --> 06:15.341
- Pardon me? - Still...

70
06:15.341 --> 06:18.159
It's got the video you took. What a relief, right?

71
06:18.810 --> 06:20.574
I don't understand.

72
06:20.574 --> 06:22.998
I mean, how did you...

73
06:22.998 --> 06:26.563
Mister, what are you, exactly?

74
06:26.563 --> 06:28.945
Wait, you're not... God, are you?

75
06:30.056 --> 06:31.373
Or an angel?

76
06:31.373 --> 06:32.628
Me?

77
06:34.123 --> 06:36.105
They call me a fairy.

78
06:42.596 --> 06:44.153
A fairy?

79
06:50.943 --> 06:52.433
Oh, right.

80
06:52.433 --> 06:53.951
I was wondering,

81
06:53.951 --> 06:56.821
if we travel back to the past again,

82
06:56.821 --> 06:59.519
will Woo Jae and I... You know...

83
06:59.519 --> 07:03.353
Will our bodies... swap again?

84
07:03.353 --> 07:05.057
Oh, that?

85
07:05.057 --> 07:06.568
No, that won't happen anymore.

86
07:06.568 --> 07:08.985
That was an honest mistake, my bad.

87
07:08.985 --> 07:10.143
I see.

88
07:10.143 --> 07:11.720
A mistake...

89
07:11.720 --> 07:12.964
A mistake?

90
07:12.964 --> 07:15.231
Did you just say "a mistake?"

91
07:16.296 --> 07:17.773
Hey, Mister!

92
07:17.773 --> 07:21.417
Because of your "honest mistake,"

93
07:21.417 --> 07:23.263
I had to wear a skirt!

94
07:23.263 --> 07:24.581
A flappy, breezy skirt!

95
07:24.581 --> 07:26.256
And don't get me started on the hair!

96
07:26.256 --> 07:27.980
This bastard confessed to me!

97
07:27.980 --> 07:29.571
It wasn't for you!

98
07:29.571 --> 07:31.595
You know what I mean.

99
07:31.595 --> 07:33.732
I can't even put it into words!

100
07:33.732 --> 07:35.779
You get me?

101
07:35.779 --> 07:37.210
You're not perfect, either.

102
07:37.210 --> 07:38.723
He's got a point.

103
07:38.723 --> 07:40.134
What?

104
07:43.610 --> 07:46.321
There you go.

105
07:46.321 --> 07:48.021
Thank you, sir.

106
08:06.508 --> 08:08.208
It's on.

107
08:10.996 --> 08:13.223
No way!

108
08:13.223 --> 08:15.097
Thank you, Mr. Fairy...

109
08:21.023 --> 08:22.983
What the...

110
08:22.983 --> 08:25.004
Was he really a fairy?

111
08:25.763 --> 08:27.730
That can't be.

112
08:27.730 --> 08:30.137
His eyes were pretty fairy-like, though.

113
08:35.850 --> 08:37.550
Thank goodness.

114
09:35.736 --> 09:38.300
I was feeling down, so I bought a yacht.

115
09:38.300 --> 09:40.190
How about a yacht party tomorrow?

116
09:40.190 --> 09:42.518
- Good for you. - What a shame.

117
09:42.518 --> 09:44.951
Our chef gets horribly seasick, you see.

118
09:44.951 --> 09:48.948
Do you know I own a building at Avenue Montaigne in Paris?

119
09:48.948 --> 09:51.685
If you want, you can open a restaurant there.

120
09:51.685 --> 09:53.216
I'll deal with all the papers.

121
09:53.216 --> 09:55.834
How's that? You want to come with me?

122
09:55.834 --> 09:58.243
Wow, Montaigne, huh?

123
09:58.243 --> 10:00.040
Now, now.

124
10:00.040 --> 10:05.488
We already have several offers under the chef's name.

125
10:05.488 --> 10:06.559
Okay?

126
10:06.559 --> 10:09.816
I'll give you my email address, and you can send me an email there.

127
10:09.816 --> 10:12.436
I'll run it through and write back.

128
10:12.436 --> 10:14.177
I will get back to you, okay?

129
10:14.177 --> 10:16.830
Here's my business card.

130
10:16.830 --> 10:18.367
Here.

131
10:18.367 --> 10:20.760
What? The hell are you talking about?

132
10:20.760 --> 10:22.479
I had it made yesterday.

133
10:28.523 --> 10:30.913
- Hey, what's wrong? - What's wrong?

134
10:30.913 --> 10:32.613
Are you okay?

135
10:38.276 --> 10:40.036
Are you alright?

136
10:40.036 --> 10:42.170
- What's wrong? - What?

137
10:42.170 --> 10:43.515
Yeah...

138
10:49.450 --> 10:52.435
I'm back to the day before the award ceremony.

139
10:53.723 --> 10:55.312
Who is it?

140
10:56.026 --> 10:57.803
Hey, Gyeong Woo!

141
10:57.803 --> 10:59.567
I need to get going!

142
10:59.567 --> 11:01.303
- Have fun! - Wait, wait!

143
11:01.303 --> 11:03.282
- Where are you going? - I'll drive you...

144
11:04.139 --> 11:06.036
I guess I won't be driving him.

145
11:06.036 --> 11:08.800
So how about we have some serious talk...

146
11:42.643 --> 11:44.954
Did I actually make it?

147
11:53.323 --> 11:55.730
The day before the ceremony...

148
11:55.730 --> 11:57.146
Ha Na.

149
11:58.523 --> 12:00.983
Where are you going? Woo Jae!

150
12:00.983 --> 12:02.495
Hey!

151
12:09.167 --> 12:11.720
Why is it so quiet in here?

152
12:52.996 --> 12:54.696
Thank goodness...

153
12:56.376 --> 12:58.076
I'm so relieved.

154
13:07.772 --> 13:12.319
So, you and Yoon Ha Na are shooting Yang Jun Mo's movie?

155
13:13.263 --> 13:16.530
Yeah, since a week ago.

156
13:16.530 --> 13:19.623
So, Park Gi Tae, who stabbed me and fled,

157
13:19.623 --> 13:22.556
and all the evidence that we had... are gone?

158
13:22.556 --> 13:24.584
And I'm in a coma?

159
13:27.392 --> 13:28.996
So...

160
13:28.996 --> 13:31.497
You all came here because of me.

161
13:32.570 --> 13:34.388
Of course we did.

162
13:36.776 --> 13:39.643
You guys are like two peas in a pod.

163
13:39.643 --> 13:42.923
Hey! Both of you, I'm sick of this!

164
13:42.923 --> 13:44.647
"It's my fault..."

165
13:44.647 --> 13:45.737
"Because of me..."

166
13:45.737 --> 13:47.961
Stop saying that! No more moping!

167
13:47.961 --> 13:49.796
I'm banning you!

168
13:49.796 --> 13:52.010
Sure, it's because of Woo Jae, and sometimes it's because of Ha Na.

169
13:52.010 --> 13:54.430
So what? Let's say it was because of me.

170
13:54.430 --> 13:57.493
Wouldn't you do the same? To save me?

171
14:00.730 --> 14:02.240
Of course we would.

172
14:02.240 --> 14:03.791
Yeah.

173
14:03.791 --> 14:05.450
See?

174
14:05.450 --> 14:07.694
So please, I'm begging you.

175
14:07.694 --> 14:09.323
Let's not be overly apologetic to each other.

176
14:09.323 --> 14:13.020
We're short on time. We literally don't have time to mope around!

177
14:13.020 --> 14:15.083
Okay?

178
14:15.083 --> 14:17.036
- Okay. - Okay.

179
14:17.036 --> 14:18.607
Perfect.

180
14:21.710 --> 14:23.627
Anyway, why did you guys hesitate?

181
14:24.313 --> 14:26.187
You'll... save me, right?

182
14:26.187 --> 14:27.593
Right?

183
14:30.830 --> 14:32.390
Where's Ha Ri?

184
14:32.390 --> 14:34.271
You should've contacted her sooner.

185
14:36.643 --> 14:38.176
By the way...

186
14:38.176 --> 14:40.697
that's not your father, you said?

187
14:40.697 --> 14:42.380
No, he isn't.

188
14:43.105 --> 14:45.216
Does he have a twin?

189
14:45.216 --> 14:48.103
We were thinking of finding out, actually.

190
14:48.103 --> 14:50.065
A hidden uncle?

191
14:50.065 --> 14:51.370
Some sort of family secret?

192
14:51.370 --> 14:54.030
But Park Gi Tae and Yang Jun Mo come first.

193
14:54.030 --> 14:55.347
You don't know anything, do you?

194
14:55.347 --> 14:58.137
- You're such an annoying... - Our clients.

195
14:58.137 --> 14:59.981
You're all very famous people, yes?

196
14:59.981 --> 15:03.843
Oh, we won't ask you for your signatures or anything.

197
15:03.843 --> 15:06.007
You can rest easy.

198
15:06.007 --> 15:08.604
- Our confidentiality policy... - Must be pretty strict.

199
15:08.604 --> 15:10.476
What say we rest assured?

200
15:10.476 --> 15:13.928
Okay. Now, shall we begin?

201
15:16.443 --> 15:17.817
Good.

202
15:55.083 --> 15:57.296
We need to secure the evidence

203
15:57.296 --> 15:58.896
before Yang Jun Mo can get rid of it.

204
15:58.896 --> 16:01.109
First, see that the ceremony ends well.

205
16:01.109 --> 16:04.387
Just like it happened. Don't change a thing.

206
16:05.369 --> 16:09.576
Make sure not to let Yang Jun Mo get suspicious.

207
16:09.576 --> 16:15.057
The Best Actor Award of the 30th Baekryong Film Awards, 2026, goes to...

208
16:15.057 --> 16:16.900
Jung Woo Jae, from the movie "Thirties."

209
16:16.900 --> 16:18.473
Congratulations.

210
16:37.536 --> 16:41.983
First of all, I thank you all for granting me such an honorable award.

211
16:41.983 --> 16:44.237
I won't grow complacent.

212
16:44.237 --> 16:47.001
I will always be eager to learn,

213
16:47.001 --> 16:49.408
and to become an honest actor.

214
16:50.976 --> 16:52.588
Thank you.

215
17:35.776 --> 17:37.702
Do you like me that much?

216
17:43.543 --> 17:47.143
Enough to miss me as soon as you open your eyes?

217
17:48.196 --> 17:50.199
Stop it.

218
17:52.563 --> 17:55.036
- You were pretending to be asleep? - Yeah.

219
17:55.036 --> 17:56.653
I was.

220
17:56.653 --> 17:58.353
You...

221
18:24.550 --> 18:26.577
Everything should stay the same, right?

222
18:27.809 --> 18:29.273
Stay the same?

223
18:29.273 --> 18:30.917
With the past.

224
18:30.917 --> 18:32.689
You said not to change it.

225
18:34.716 --> 18:36.944
This past is known only to me.

226
18:37.716 --> 18:39.416
I'll lead you. Just trust me.

227
19:06.376 --> 19:08.723
Emotional... paralysis?

228
19:08.723 --> 19:09.781
What's that?

229
19:09.781 --> 19:14.489
My brain can't process emotions like happiness, sadness, and even surprise.

230
19:14.489 --> 19:16.800
It has a delayed response to feelings.

231
19:16.800 --> 19:19.120
Like an emotional short circuit.

232
19:21.290 --> 19:22.848
Ha Na.

233
19:22.848 --> 19:24.874
Are you okay?

234
19:24.874 --> 19:29.578
My brain can't process emotions like happiness, sadness, and even surprise.

235
19:29.578 --> 19:31.587
It has a delayed response to feelings.

236
19:31.587 --> 19:33.716
Like an emotional short circuit.

237
19:33.716 --> 19:35.416
Emotional...

238
19:36.149 --> 19:37.632
paralysis?

239
19:45.496 --> 19:47.196
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

240
19:47.856 --> 19:50.916
- You should get a new actress for the role. - No.

241
19:54.136 --> 19:55.660
First things first.

242
19:55.660 --> 19:57.631
You should focus on recovery.

243
19:57.631 --> 19:59.955
- Jun Mo. - It has to be you.

244
20:00.710 --> 20:04.110
Nobody else will suffice. Never. It would be pointless.

245
20:04.110 --> 20:05.920
So empty your mind.

246
20:05.920 --> 20:07.930
Just focus on yourself.

247
20:07.930 --> 20:09.630
On your recovery.

248
20:10.223 --> 20:12.349
I'll wait for however long it takes.

249
20:12.936 --> 20:14.636
It's fine, really.

250
20:16.856 --> 20:18.220
Jun Mo.

251
20:18.870 --> 20:19.916
Yes?

252
20:19.916 --> 20:24.637
I know how I shine in the frame that you create.

253
20:24.637 --> 20:26.831
I know it well.

254
20:27.472 --> 20:29.703
For that, I am infinitely thankful.

255
20:29.703 --> 20:31.403
It's an honor.

256
20:32.379 --> 20:35.107
- You're making me blush. - However,

257
20:35.107 --> 20:37.691
your film will shine anyway, even without me.

258
20:37.691 --> 20:39.328
I, too,

259
20:39.328 --> 20:41.772
will shine just as brightly without your movie.

260
20:41.772 --> 20:43.147
Ha Na...

261
20:43.774 --> 20:46.520
- That's not... - The world that you create

262
20:46.520 --> 20:49.017
won't waver without me.

263
20:49.017 --> 20:50.743
I truly wish with all my heart,

264
20:50.743 --> 20:55.025
that you become a renowned director who is loved for a long time.

265
21:00.599 --> 21:03.859
You don't have to pretend to be okay in front of me.

266
21:03.859 --> 21:05.230
Ha Na.

267
21:05.230 --> 21:07.467
You're the best actress in my eyes.

268
21:07.467 --> 21:09.078
Whatever anyone else says,

269
21:09.078 --> 21:11.426
you are the best ever, at least in my life.

270
21:11.426 --> 21:14.310
You, Ha Na, are the best actress ever, at least to me.

271
21:14.310 --> 21:17.259
You'll get better soon. Don't worry.

272
21:17.259 --> 21:18.732
Understood?

273
22:14.506 --> 22:16.614
It's begun again.

274
22:28.426 --> 22:30.788
Ha Na, did you sleep well?

275
22:32.390 --> 22:33.814
Should we, like...

276
22:33.814 --> 22:36.145
send it back, or something?

277
22:57.046 --> 22:58.482
Ha Na!

278
22:59.226 --> 23:01.826
- Ha Na! - What, what is it?

279
23:01.826 --> 23:03.270
What's wrong, Ha Na?

280
23:03.270 --> 23:04.757
Are you okay?

281
23:08.699 --> 23:10.399
Hey, Jung Woo Jae!

282
23:27.693 --> 23:29.168
Yoon Ha Na!

283
23:40.086 --> 23:41.926
I'm sorry, Jun Mo.

284
23:41.926 --> 23:44.851
Having to stop the production a week after starting...

285
23:45.989 --> 23:49.426
I have no words to defend myself.

286
23:49.426 --> 23:52.999
It's fine. It's not like it was your fault.

287
23:52.999 --> 23:56.986
I spoke with the production company, so don't worry about it.

288
23:56.986 --> 24:00.521
- Just focus on Ha Na's recovery. - Thank you so much.

289
24:01.733 --> 24:05.059
Bad things have been happening to Ha Na lately.

290
24:05.059 --> 24:07.392
It's driving me mad, too.

291
24:07.392 --> 24:08.676
Oh, right.

292
24:08.676 --> 24:14.171
They even found toxic chemicals in the banana milk Ha Na had in her fridge!

293
24:20.773 --> 24:22.630
Did you report it to the police?

294
24:22.630 --> 24:25.687
Well, they said they'd take care of it,

295
24:25.687 --> 24:27.981
but we still haven't heard back from them.

296
25:16.133 --> 25:19.893
[Great, let's proceed. I've paid up front.] [Let me know when you're ready.]

297
25:27.099 --> 25:29.826
[Is there a problem?]

298
25:48.126 --> 25:50.803
Shut up for once!

299
26:16.887 --> 26:17.889
[Woo Jae's Father]

300
26:27.808 --> 26:30.939
Hello, sir. How are you doing?

301
26:41.623 --> 26:43.093
There you are.

302
26:45.154 --> 26:48.254
I changed the code, and installed a new lock on the front door.

303
26:48.254 --> 26:50.238
They won't get back in here.

304
26:50.238 --> 26:51.962
Thank you, Woo Jae.

305
26:51.962 --> 26:53.674
You did well.

306
26:53.674 --> 26:55.345
It's nothing.

307
26:55.345 --> 26:56.738
Are you okay?

308
26:59.099 --> 27:01.792
I have some business to see to.

309
27:01.792 --> 27:03.492
I'll leave you to it.

310
27:04.686 --> 27:06.200
Go on.

311
27:10.054 --> 27:12.091
- Shall we? - Yeah.

312
27:14.581 --> 27:16.372
Look here! Look at me!

313
27:16.372 --> 27:18.968
Here, birdie, birdie!

314
27:18.968 --> 27:22.044
It's looking a bit limp.

315
27:24.328 --> 27:27.901
I assume you like this bird, Director Yang?

316
27:27.901 --> 27:30.528
I do. Pretty, isn't it?

317
27:30.528 --> 27:32.894
- Ha Na. - Yes?

318
27:32.894 --> 27:35.194
- Cute. - Why don't we run somewhere far away?

319
27:35.194 --> 27:36.645
Run away?

320
27:37.252 --> 27:40.348
We can go somewhere where nobody knows us,

321
27:40.348 --> 27:42.246
and live a life like any other.

322
27:42.848 --> 27:44.453
A normal life.

323
27:45.114 --> 27:46.848
A normal life?

324
27:46.848 --> 27:49.785
We'll wake up together in the morning,

325
27:49.785 --> 27:51.650
maybe bicker around,

326
27:51.650 --> 27:55.468
then by dinner, we'll share a beer and a laugh,

327
27:55.468 --> 27:57.568
and fall asleep together by night.

328
27:58.434 --> 28:01.834
A place where nobody knows the global star Jung Woo Jae?

329
28:01.834 --> 28:04.057
Is that even a place on earth?

330
28:05.921 --> 28:07.294
I...

331
28:07.948 --> 28:09.945
don't have to be an actor.

332
28:17.401 --> 28:19.525
- What? - I mean it.

333
28:19.525 --> 28:21.249
You're all I need.

334
28:21.249 --> 28:23.553
- Woo Jae. - Emotional paralysis.

335
28:23.553 --> 28:26.584
It's caused by suppressing your feelings, isn't it?

336
28:26.584 --> 28:30.352
I want you to laugh when you're happy,

337
28:30.352 --> 28:33.148
and get angry when you're sad.

338
28:33.148 --> 28:35.372
That's all I wish for.

339
28:35.372 --> 28:38.255
I'm being serious, Ha Na.

340
28:38.968 --> 28:41.912
I should've given you a call sooner, sir.

341
28:41.912 --> 28:45.257
I was just too busy, my apologies.

342
28:45.257 --> 28:47.805
Oh, we're way past that stage of our friendship, I'm sure.

343
28:47.805 --> 28:49.649
You're working with my son.

344
28:49.649 --> 28:52.533
That means we're like family, doesn't it?

345
28:52.533 --> 28:54.348
I'm glad you think so.

346
28:54.348 --> 28:58.171
I'm always grateful for you, you know.

347
29:07.194 --> 29:09.034
You should know when to stop.

348
29:09.034 --> 29:10.734
Don't ever reach out to me again.

349
29:13.654 --> 29:16.288
That ungrateful bastard...

350
29:17.181 --> 29:18.481
Hey, son!

351
29:18.481 --> 29:20.879
I'll call you later!

352
29:30.228 --> 29:32.363
Are you... Woo Jae's father?

353
29:36.234 --> 29:38.685
- Who... - It's great to meet you.

354
29:38.685 --> 29:41.208
I'm Yang Jun Mo, a movie director.

355
29:43.057 --> 29:44.609
- Director Yang Jun Mo! - Yes, sir.

356
29:44.609 --> 29:47.388
Director Yang! It's nice to meet you.

357
29:48.028 --> 29:49.568
Nice to meet you, sir.

358
29:54.374 --> 29:56.098
It's nothing.

359
29:56.098 --> 29:58.829
My own darn son won't even answer my calls,

360
29:58.829 --> 30:02.878
but you check in on me, and give me money as well.

361
30:03.581 --> 30:05.281
Of course I'm grateful.

362
30:06.188 --> 30:08.098
Hey, by the way.

363
30:08.098 --> 30:09.662
I heard the movie got canceled.

364
30:09.662 --> 30:12.273
- I heard you suffered some heavy losses. - I'm alright.

365
30:12.273 --> 30:14.290
The actors' health comes first.

366
30:14.290 --> 30:17.208
In fact, I'm really enjoying my time off.

367
30:17.208 --> 30:19.758
It's nice that I have time to see you.

368
30:28.054 --> 30:31.775
Right, are you having any trouble recently?

369
30:37.255 --> 30:38.711
Well...

370
30:40.415 --> 30:41.813
Actually,

371
30:42.475 --> 30:45.153
can I borrow some money?

372
30:45.864 --> 30:50.474
- You know my kid will pay you back if I can't. - Alright, Woo Jae. Let's run away together.

373
30:52.206 --> 30:53.712
Sir.

374
30:55.466 --> 30:58.143
I have a better idea.

375
31:04.613 --> 31:06.313
Alright, okay!

376
31:08.019 --> 31:12.079
I already took care of Ha Na's schedule, so there's no need to worry.

377
31:12.079 --> 31:14.497
But things are different for Woo Jae.

378
31:14.497 --> 31:16.213
You can't leave straight away.

379
31:16.213 --> 31:18.733
I'll do my best to make it quick.

380
31:18.733 --> 31:22.721
But you still need to see your pre-planned schedule through to the end.

381
31:23.360 --> 31:26.900
Of course. Thank you for understanding.

382
31:26.900 --> 31:28.790
Ye Rang,

383
31:28.790 --> 31:30.837
I have so much to thank you for.

384
31:32.293 --> 31:34.764
Well, you only wish to be happy.

385
31:34.764 --> 31:36.819
What else can I do?

386
31:37.421 --> 31:39.758
So, both of you,

387
31:39.758 --> 31:42.297
make sure that you end up happy.

388
31:42.297 --> 31:44.783
- Ye Rang... - That's that, then!

389
31:44.783 --> 31:46.569
If you ever change your mind,

390
31:46.569 --> 31:48.647
and wish to return...

391
31:48.647 --> 31:50.660
just promise me.

392
31:51.449 --> 31:53.916
Promise to come back to me.

393
31:53.916 --> 31:55.487
Both of you.

394
31:55.487 --> 31:56.825
Yes.

395
31:58.621 --> 31:59.883
Good.

396
32:35.016 --> 32:37.613
We'll start with the product name.

397
32:37.613 --> 32:40.737
Your right side looks best, so we'll focus on that side.

398
32:40.737 --> 32:43.168
- Let's get ready. - His left side is amazing, too.

399
32:43.168 --> 32:44.576
We'll get that side, too.

400
32:44.576 --> 32:46.348
Thank you.

401
32:46.348 --> 32:48.163
- This is perfect. - Woo Jae.

402
32:48.163 --> 32:49.853
You look stunning today.

403
32:49.853 --> 32:51.284
- Really? - Really.

404
32:51.284 --> 32:53.508
Could we touch up his makeup?

405
32:55.828 --> 32:57.848
Outsiders are prohibited!

406
32:57.848 --> 33:00.524
Hey, Woo Jae! It's your dad!

407
33:00.524 --> 33:01.992
What the hell.

408
33:01.992 --> 33:03.350
My boy.

409
33:03.350 --> 33:06.754
Your dad's weeping tears of blood from poverty,

410
33:06.754 --> 33:10.061
and you're frolicking around posing for pictures?

411
33:10.720 --> 33:12.922
Sir, if you would just talk to me...

412
33:12.922 --> 33:15.342
- What's there to talk about? - I'll take care of it.

413
33:15.342 --> 33:16.420
- Soo Hyuk! - Yes!

414
33:16.420 --> 33:17.764
- Let's talk outside. - Outside?

415
33:17.764 --> 33:19.935
- Let's go! - What do you mean, "take care of?"

416
33:19.935 --> 33:23.389
Tell me how you're going to "take care of it!"

417
33:25.908 --> 33:29.436
And you're frolicking around posing for pictures?

418
33:29.436 --> 33:32.629
[Is Jung Woo Jae a neglectful son?] Sir, if you would just talk to me...

419
33:32.629 --> 33:34.049
What's there to talk about?

420
33:34.049 --> 33:35.936
I'll take care of it.

421
33:35.936 --> 33:36.976
- Soo Hyuk! - Yes!

422
33:36.976 --> 33:38.260
- Let's talk outside. - Outside?

423
33:38.260 --> 33:40.210
- Let's go! - What do you mean, "take care of?"

424
33:40.210 --> 33:41.894
So this...

425
33:41.894 --> 33:44.764
didn't happen originally, right?

426
33:47.589 --> 33:49.289
Are you okay?

427
33:51.896 --> 33:53.219
Yeah.

428
34:06.148 --> 34:09.234
It was going to happen one day or another.

429
34:09.234 --> 34:12.009
I'm fine. Don't worry.

430
34:16.575 --> 34:19.306
[The grisly truth about the fan-favorite actor Jung Woo Jae's childhood revealed?]

431
34:29.269 --> 34:31.968
Well, thanks to you...

432
34:31.968 --> 34:36.415
I got a pretty penny's worth of allowance from my dear boy.

433
34:38.496 --> 34:40.920
It's nothing, sir.

434
34:40.920 --> 34:42.563
Woo Jae must've been surprised.

435
34:42.563 --> 34:44.263
Exactly, yeah.

436
34:46.023 --> 34:48.310
But...

437
34:48.310 --> 34:52.427
A person may seem like some great artist to any observer,

438
34:52.427 --> 34:54.733
but people are all the same.

439
34:56.696 --> 34:58.077
Excuse me?

440
35:00.656 --> 35:03.067
I mean, you and I,

441
35:03.067 --> 35:04.724
we're the same scum of the earth.

442
35:04.724 --> 35:06.448
Don't you agree?

443
35:06.448 --> 35:08.419
Consider us equal from now on.

444
35:08.419 --> 35:12.240
I'd be glad to teach my son a lesson every now and then.

445
35:13.943 --> 35:17.606
I don't understand what you mean.

446
35:27.616 --> 35:30.500
You think today's the only time I did this?

447
35:30.500 --> 35:33.914
Woo Jae shouldn't have abandoned you like this.

448
35:39.316 --> 35:42.480
Woo Jae is shooting an advertisement tomorrow.

449
35:42.480 --> 35:44.328
Why don't you give him a visit?

450
35:45.090 --> 35:48.397
Teach him that he should take better care of you.

451
35:50.950 --> 35:53.157
A fatherly life lesson, so to speak.

452
35:58.469 --> 36:01.617
Let me check the time.

453
36:14.883 --> 36:17.174
You must've been frustrated about your movie.

454
36:17.174 --> 36:20.018
You wanted to screw my son over, didn't you?

455
36:20.018 --> 36:23.232
Isn't that why you paid me?

456
36:26.696 --> 36:29.935
I want you to have a pretty sum ready for me.

457
36:34.136 --> 36:38.320
And get some good whiskey, like a Royal Ballantine's 30 years.

458
36:38.320 --> 36:41.102
My taste buds are sophisticated, believe it or not.

459
36:42.296 --> 36:43.706
Got it?

460
36:43.706 --> 36:48.464
Serving me some darn crappy whiskey...

461
37:18.743 --> 37:22.366
Sorry for the delay. Are there any changes to the contract?

462
37:29.836 --> 37:32.276
Hey, Woo Jae! It's your dad!

463
37:33.330 --> 37:35.389
My boy.

464
37:35.389 --> 37:37.344
Your dad's weeping tears of blood from poverty,

465
37:37.344 --> 37:39.070
[CEO Seo Ye Rang]

466
37:39.070 --> 37:42.364
and you're frolicking around posing for pictures?

467
37:43.723 --> 37:46.207
Hi, CEO Seo.

468
37:46.207 --> 37:49.304
Woo Jae and Ha Na are with each other right now, right?

469
37:49.304 --> 37:51.028
Yeah, why do you ask?

470
37:51.028 --> 37:53.211
They're both not picking up.

471
37:53.211 --> 37:54.643
Just checking in.

472
37:54.643 --> 37:56.736
If they're together, that's fine.

473
37:58.423 --> 38:00.530
Hey, you...

474
38:01.243 --> 38:03.800
Are you alright, Ye Rang?

475
38:03.800 --> 38:05.331
The company must be a mess, too.

476
38:05.331 --> 38:08.054
Not the time to worry about me. I'm hanging up.

477
38:15.056 --> 38:18.918
If you don't want to ruin what we have now,

478
38:18.918 --> 38:21.734
then at least show me... a little respect.

479
38:22.672 --> 38:24.427
Seo Ye Rang...

480
38:27.052 --> 38:28.959
[Han Soo Hyuk]

481
38:31.192 --> 38:32.423
Hello?

482
38:32.423 --> 38:34.327
- Hey, Soo Hyuk. - Yes?

483
38:34.327 --> 38:37.771
I'm planning to cook some burnt rice and braised beef.

484
38:37.771 --> 38:40.402
Could you take some over to CEO Seo?

485
38:40.402 --> 38:44.096
She can't stomach food when she's stressed.

486
38:44.096 --> 38:45.760
I just know she's starving herself again.

487
38:45.760 --> 38:48.363
You're not wrong. But...

488
38:48.363 --> 38:51.340
Ye Rang's meeting up with Kang Do Hoon for dinner today.

489
38:51.340 --> 38:54.224
He's acting really suspicious.

490
38:54.224 --> 38:55.948
Guess where they're meeting.

491
38:55.948 --> 38:58.179
- Where? - Namsan Hotel!

492
38:58.179 --> 38:59.863
That's where they first met!

493
38:59.863 --> 39:02.260
I can feel it. He's going to propose!

494
39:02.260 --> 39:04.069
He's... proposing?

495
39:10.483 --> 39:12.034
Nine years ago,

496
39:12.034 --> 39:14.871
I first met you here. And since then...

497
39:14.871 --> 39:18.001
my love for you has never changed.

498
39:18.963 --> 39:20.361
Do Hoon...

499
39:21.330 --> 39:25.416
Will you... marry me?

500
39:25.416 --> 39:27.974
All your past, and all your pain...

501
39:27.974 --> 39:29.963
I want to bear it for you.

502
39:29.963 --> 39:32.930
So that you never feel lonely in this world we live in...

503
39:32.930 --> 39:34.630
I'll be there.

504
39:41.310 --> 39:42.633
Do Hoon.

505
40:14.616 --> 40:16.124
This...

506
40:16.903 --> 40:18.913
is my golden goose.

507
40:22.596 --> 40:24.870
Director Yang, I'm touched.

508
40:24.870 --> 40:27.911
You treat me so well.

509
40:42.536 --> 40:44.953
Are you goddamn kidding me?

510
40:48.003 --> 40:49.154
See this?

511
40:49.154 --> 40:51.911
What do you think would happen if I leaked this to the press?

512
40:51.911 --> 40:54.202
Movie director Yang Jun Mo will be over.

513
40:54.202 --> 40:56.719
You'll fall to your demise in a heartbeat.

514
41:00.017 --> 41:01.744
I'm sure you have lots to lose.

515
41:01.744 --> 41:04.590
So why are you being so stingy?

516
41:06.330 --> 41:07.773
Sir.

517
41:08.964 --> 41:13.005
Do you know what I hate the most?

518
41:13.005 --> 41:14.409
What?

519
41:15.130 --> 41:17.490
- Mistakes. - Mistakes?

520
41:17.490 --> 41:19.214
Yes.

521
41:19.214 --> 41:20.632
Well, I...

522
41:20.632 --> 41:23.554
I just can't stand the mistakes that I've made.

523
41:36.004 --> 41:38.126
You made your bed, now lie in it.

524
41:39.330 --> 41:41.634
If it's your mess,

525
41:41.634 --> 41:43.717
you should clean it up.

526
41:44.350 --> 41:46.180
Squeaky-clean.

527
41:56.537 --> 41:58.069
Exactly.

528
42:02.777 --> 42:04.477
You're right.

529
42:18.530 --> 42:20.635
I should clean it up.

530
42:22.630 --> 42:24.330
Squeaky-clean.

531
42:38.610 --> 42:40.481
Are you scared?

532
42:40.481 --> 42:42.205
It caught me by surprise.

533
42:42.205 --> 42:43.590
It's okay.

534
42:46.057 --> 42:48.866
I wish time would stop like this.

535
42:51.197 --> 42:52.682
Will we...

536
42:54.444 --> 42:56.528
really be okay?

537
42:57.477 --> 42:58.796
Yes.

538
42:59.810 --> 43:01.481
We'll be alright.

539
43:01.481 --> 43:03.319
Don't worry.

540
43:04.170 --> 43:05.461
You know me.

541
43:05.461 --> 43:07.382
I'm the Yoon Ha Na.

542
43:18.220 --> 43:19.470
[Dad]

543
43:19.470 --> 43:21.977
[Son]

544
43:37.731 --> 43:39.690
The person you are calling is unavailable...

545
43:39.690 --> 43:41.390
Not picking up?

546
43:42.984 --> 43:44.289
Yeah.

547
43:45.630 --> 43:47.703
I bet he's drinking.

548
44:02.184 --> 44:04.080
You made your bed...

549
44:05.064 --> 44:06.764
Now lie in it.

550
44:33.110 --> 44:35.417
This is your last task.

551
44:35.417 --> 44:37.993
Make sure you make no mistakes.

552
44:52.924 --> 44:55.094
Take a rest while I pack.

553
44:55.094 --> 44:56.997
I'll be quick.

554
44:56.997 --> 44:58.621
Our flight leaves in the early morning. We have enough time.

555
44:58.621 --> 45:01.067
Take your time, and be careful.

556
45:05.010 --> 45:07.637
- I'll be back. - Okay.

557
45:07.637 --> 45:09.274
- See you later. - Stay inside.

558
45:09.274 --> 45:10.664
Okay.

559
45:23.806 --> 45:25.547
[Woo]

560
45:28.384 --> 45:31.690
Sorry, I fell asleep.

561
45:31.690 --> 45:33.115
Now?

562
45:34.444 --> 45:37.563
Yeah, I'm in the parking lot now.

563
45:38.237 --> 45:40.977
It's fine, I'll get there soon enough.

564
45:40.977 --> 45:43.304
Okay. Talk to you later.

565
45:46.457 --> 45:48.029
Ms. Yoon Ha Na.

566
47:11.744 --> 47:13.444
Jun Mo...

567
47:30.621 --> 47:32.408
Where were you running off to?

568
47:32.408 --> 47:34.325
Running away?

569
47:34.325 --> 47:36.902
Please, stop now.

570
47:36.902 --> 47:39.440
You're about to cross the point of no return.

571
47:39.440 --> 47:41.329
Tell me, why...

572
47:52.404 --> 47:54.384
It's all because of you.

573
47:54.384 --> 47:56.034
What?

574
47:56.034 --> 48:00.378
You came from the future and messed with my movie, and my life.

575
48:00.378 --> 48:01.956
Do you have any idea...

576
48:01.956 --> 48:04.276
how long I've waited for you?

577
48:05.910 --> 48:07.759
Emotional paralysis?

578
48:09.237 --> 48:10.488
Leaving?

579
48:10.488 --> 48:12.361
Quitting acting?

580
48:18.837 --> 48:21.474
The camcorder is in my hands,

581
48:21.474 --> 48:23.982
yet you're still traveling through time. How?

582
48:32.424 --> 48:34.948
Isn't the camcorder the time machine?

583
48:34.948 --> 48:36.538
Or was it you all this time?

584
48:38.044 --> 48:40.327
Do I need to kill you to bring this to an end?

585
49:02.077 --> 49:04.595
Get it together, Yang Jun Mo.

586
49:12.597 --> 49:14.145
I'll...

587
49:14.797 --> 49:16.747
put an end to this.

588
49:18.837 --> 49:21.050
You're what made me do this.

589
49:22.670 --> 49:24.370
Don't blame me for it.

590
49:29.384 --> 49:32.794
The first thing you'll notice is that you've lost your voice.

591
49:32.794 --> 49:36.276
Everything will become an afterimage that'll last longer.

592
49:37.857 --> 49:41.395
This music, and my voice, they'll all fade away.

593
49:41.395 --> 49:43.094
And slowly...

594
49:43.784 --> 49:47.233
you'll lose all feeling in every fiber of your body.

595
49:49.117 --> 49:51.841
Finally, you'll forget how to breathe.

596
49:51.841 --> 49:54.078
It'll be a very deep,

597
49:54.078 --> 49:56.140
and peaceful sleep.

598
49:56.140 --> 49:59.044
Your heart will come to a quiet stop.

599
49:59.704 --> 50:01.108
What do you think?

600
50:01.108 --> 50:03.257
Sounds so serene, doesn't it?

601
50:14.337 --> 50:15.777
Ha Na!

602
50:19.630 --> 50:21.659
How did you find this place?

603
50:25.330 --> 50:28.274
Are you sure you can do it?

604
50:28.274 --> 50:31.825
Don't question it. If it's to save Ha Na and Woo Jae,

605
50:31.825 --> 50:33.958
what is there not to do?

606
50:45.017 --> 50:46.428
Okay.

607
50:50.917 --> 50:53.614
- I need to use the restroom. - Sure, Jun Mo.

608
50:53.614 --> 50:55.332
Where's the toilet?

609
50:55.332 --> 50:57.599
I'll show you to it, sir.

610
50:58.897 --> 51:00.874
You're drunk, aren't you?

611
51:00.874 --> 51:02.574
You're hammered!

612
51:03.544 --> 51:05.579
Safe travels, Jun Mo!

613
51:23.610 --> 51:25.644
Come on, please work...

614
51:31.477 --> 51:32.959
It worked!

615
51:45.773 --> 51:48.130
Hey, Jun Mo!

616
51:48.130 --> 51:49.864
Are you drunk?

617
51:52.404 --> 51:54.917
Get over here, take a shot!

618
51:54.917 --> 51:57.161
You haven't changed, Seo Ye Rang.

619
51:57.161 --> 51:58.972
- You've still got it. - Jun Mo.

620
51:58.972 --> 52:00.602
We're going full-out today.

621
52:00.602 --> 52:03.064
- Bottoms up. - Bottoms up!

622
52:21.272 --> 52:23.711
Is it done?

623
52:42.424 --> 52:43.917
Are you okay?

624
52:58.324 --> 52:59.773
What's this?

625
53:01.804 --> 53:03.318
You're crying.

626
53:07.097 --> 53:09.010
What the hell is this?

627
53:10.557 --> 53:12.934
What did you do to me?

628
53:15.337 --> 53:17.037
Did you lie to me?

629
53:35.070 --> 53:36.817
What's your problem?

630
53:36.817 --> 53:38.614
- It's just nice to see you. - Sure, me too.

631
53:38.614 --> 53:40.452
- Yeah, okay. - Very nice, yeah.

632
53:40.452 --> 53:42.596
- Don't follow me. - How are you doing these days?

633
53:42.596 --> 53:45.178
- I'm doing fine. - I see...

634
53:50.626 --> 53:52.557
Okay.

635
54:07.610 --> 54:08.984
See here.

636
54:08.984 --> 54:13.918
Press this, and the light comes on. That means it's on.

637
54:13.918 --> 54:18.812
Press it again, and the light turns off, which means it's not listening in anymore.

638
54:19.504 --> 54:21.434
- Feel free to make use of it. - Okay.

639
54:21.434 --> 54:23.345
Think of it as your own.

640
54:23.345 --> 54:25.548
- Thank you. - Got it.

641
54:28.957 --> 54:31.048
- Try it out. - Okay.

642
54:31.048 --> 54:32.525
This... emotional paralysis.

643
54:32.525 --> 54:34.958
Is it possible to act it out?

644
54:34.958 --> 54:38.409
My concern, exactly. Your temper is one to behold.

645
54:38.409 --> 54:40.193
- It won't be easy to fake it. - Hey.

646
54:40.193 --> 54:41.977
This is Yoon Ha Na we're talking about.

647
54:41.977 --> 54:43.701
She's good, you know.

648
54:43.701 --> 54:46.276
She already secured a diagnosis.

649
55:11.737 --> 55:14.561
Emotional... paralysis?

650
55:15.210 --> 55:16.634
What's that?

651
55:16.634 --> 55:21.122
My brain can't process emotions like happiness, sadness, and even surprise.

652
55:21.122 --> 55:23.563
It has a delayed response to feelings.

653
55:32.119 --> 55:33.972
[Banana milk]

654
55:42.012 --> 55:43.303
Ha Na!

655
55:43.303 --> 55:44.947
- Ha Na! - What, what is it?

656
55:44.947 --> 55:46.647
What's wrong, Ha Na?

657
55:48.326 --> 55:49.910
Hey, Jung Woo Jae.

658
55:51.492 --> 55:53.056
- Call emergency services. - Okay!

659
55:53.056 --> 55:54.525
My phone...

660
55:58.986 --> 56:00.686
The wiretap!

661
56:24.279 --> 56:26.714
You can't do this.

662
56:45.692 --> 56:47.252
No...

663
56:47.252 --> 56:48.952
No!

664
56:51.432 --> 56:52.894
No...

665
56:54.866 --> 56:56.310
Stop whining.

666
56:56.310 --> 56:58.010
It's just saline.

667
57:05.432 --> 57:07.486
Hi, Park Gi Tae.

668
57:07.486 --> 57:09.452
So we meet again.

669
57:09.452 --> 57:11.152
Nice to see you, Park Gi Tae.

670
57:14.886 --> 57:16.586
Hey, Yoon Ha Ru!

671
57:55.626 --> 57:57.216
Yoon Ha Ru...

672
57:58.646 --> 58:00.102
Sorry.

673
58:03.726 --> 58:05.267
Are you okay?

674
58:05.267 --> 58:06.767
I'm fine.

675
58:40.806 --> 58:42.992
You're a good fighter, Woo Jae.

676
58:45.412 --> 58:47.730
This is a problem.

677
58:47.730 --> 58:53.151
It seems that Mr. Gi Tae will take the blame for Jun Mo's crimes if we let this play out.

678
58:53.151 --> 58:57.052
Aggravated intimidation and attempted murder...

679
58:57.052 --> 58:59.930
That'll land you in jail for at least 20 years, or even a life sentence.

680
58:59.930 --> 59:01.360
What a shame.

681
59:01.967 --> 59:03.096
But...

682
59:03.096 --> 59:04.714
If you cooperate with us,

683
59:04.714 --> 59:07.458
I'll fabricate a mitigating factor to reduce your sentence.

684
59:07.458 --> 59:12.739
If the jury likes what they hear, you may be freed way sooner than you'd expect.

685
59:12.739 --> 59:14.450
How does that sound?

686
59:14.450 --> 59:16.159
Park Gi Tae.

687
59:16.159 --> 59:18.456
If you help us out this once,

688
59:18.456 --> 59:20.212
you can start anew.

689
59:20.212 --> 59:23.756
Or you can face the full consequences of all your previous murders and attempts,

690
59:23.756 --> 59:27.627
and take the bullet for Jun Mo just to rot in jail.

691
59:27.627 --> 59:29.504
Don't even think about running away.

692
59:29.504 --> 59:32.072
We'll find you anyway if we put our minds to it.

693
59:32.072 --> 59:34.290
You seem like a good guy, come on. Stand up.

694
59:34.290 --> 59:37.113
It's okay, stand up. Up, boy, up.

695
59:37.772 --> 59:39.687
That's better.

696
59:55.909 --> 59:58.143
I'm sure you already know...

697
59:58.143 --> 01:00:00.563
what you have to do.

698
01:00:09.819 --> 01:00:11.715
You guys are...

699
01:00:12.426 --> 01:00:14.842
absolutely oblivious, aren't you?

700
01:00:17.552 --> 01:00:19.752
I'm the one...

701
01:00:20.479 --> 01:00:25.065
who saved you from the vermin of this world, the lowest of the low!

702
01:00:25.065 --> 01:00:27.631
I did that!

703
01:00:28.562 --> 01:00:31.409
I'm the good guy, the protector of the story.

704
01:00:31.409 --> 01:00:33.953
You're delusional, Yang Jun Mo.

705
01:00:35.342 --> 01:00:37.660
The good guy? The protector?

706
01:00:37.660 --> 01:00:41.090
Stop trying to make it sound pretty, and face the truth.

707
01:00:41.090 --> 01:00:43.501
You didn't save anyone.

708
01:00:43.501 --> 01:00:45.312
You didn't create art.

709
01:00:45.312 --> 01:00:48.429
It's just your pathetic possessiveness...

710
01:00:48.429 --> 01:00:50.129
and obsession.

711
01:00:51.449 --> 01:00:55.780
Humans can never become a god.

712
01:00:55.780 --> 01:00:58.504
So just stop this,

713
01:00:58.504 --> 01:01:00.830
and wake up from your delusions of grandeur.

714
01:01:04.122 --> 01:01:06.584
Protect yourself first.

715
01:01:06.584 --> 01:01:08.345
No.

716
01:01:08.345 --> 01:01:10.269
I'm different.

717
01:01:10.269 --> 01:01:14.216
I'm your savior, you imperfect and flawed creatures.

718
01:01:14.216 --> 01:01:15.740
Delusions of grandeur?

719
01:01:15.740 --> 01:01:17.317
No.

720
01:01:17.317 --> 01:01:20.218
This is artistry, nearing perfection.

721
01:01:21.856 --> 01:01:25.613
You're worth nothing outside of my frame.

722
01:01:25.613 --> 01:01:28.153
You're over without me.

723
01:01:29.136 --> 01:01:30.540
You're the one who's over.

724
01:01:30.540 --> 01:01:32.532
Nonsense!

725
01:01:34.696 --> 01:01:37.077
The ending that you made...

726
01:01:39.622 --> 01:01:41.503
Aren't you curious?

727
01:01:56.736 --> 01:01:58.436
There we are.

728
01:02:00.849 --> 01:02:03.537
- The quality is surprisingly good. - Sure is.

729
01:02:08.676 --> 01:02:11.457
- Is it showing up well? - Yeah, look at this.

730
01:02:13.349 --> 01:02:15.049
It's pretty clear, right?

731
01:02:20.602 --> 01:02:22.177
This is it.

732
01:02:22.177 --> 01:02:24.774
[What a creep, can't believe I liked his movies] [That's not love, absolutely vile!]

733
01:02:24.774 --> 01:02:26.351
[I just saw the video, I'm shaking!] [Is this real?]

734
01:02:26.351 --> 01:02:28.278
[Is this what he meant by "muse?"] [I'm so creeped out I can't sleep!]

735
01:02:31.662 --> 01:02:33.686
It's over now.

736
01:02:44.990 --> 01:02:46.259
No.

737
01:03:04.596 --> 01:03:06.296
Yang Jun Mo!

738
01:03:08.729 --> 01:03:10.570
Stay back.

739
01:03:21.682 --> 01:03:23.762
You've ruined me.

740
01:03:23.762 --> 01:03:24.940
Yang Jun Mo.

741
01:03:24.940 --> 01:03:26.724
Give up and pay for your crimes.

742
01:03:26.724 --> 01:03:29.301
And keep on living, but properly this time.

743
01:03:29.301 --> 01:03:31.001
Such a tragedy.

744
01:03:31.729 --> 01:03:34.765
Mere creations, betraying the creator...

745
01:03:35.449 --> 01:03:37.553
You've wrought this hell with your own hands.

746
01:03:37.553 --> 01:03:41.013
- Stop this, Yang Jun Mo. - I'll decide my own fate.

747
01:03:43.596 --> 01:03:45.593
I'm leaving this hellhole.

748
01:03:45.593 --> 01:03:48.130
If you jump now,

749
01:03:48.130 --> 01:03:50.988
what will the world remember you as?

750
01:03:50.988 --> 01:03:55.109
You won't be the ingenious movie director Yang Jun Mo, but a criminal.

751
01:03:55.109 --> 01:04:00.240
Or maybe you'll be Yang Jun Mo, history's most pathetic director.

752
01:04:00.976 --> 01:04:04.953
Is that... what you've dreamt of?

753
01:04:06.229 --> 01:04:08.276
You know it isn't.

754
01:04:41.189 --> 01:04:43.246
Come down with us.

755
01:04:43.246 --> 01:04:44.807
Jun Mo.

756
01:05:33.282 --> 01:05:34.982
Stand back!

757
01:05:38.229 --> 01:05:40.266
If you hadn't abandoned my world...

758
01:05:40.266 --> 01:05:42.544
If you hadn't abandoned me...

759
01:05:42.544 --> 01:05:45.194
If not only for that damn camcorder!

760
01:05:45.194 --> 01:05:47.265
This is all your fault, Yoon Ha Na.

761
01:05:47.265 --> 01:05:48.965
Die!

762
01:05:50.616 --> 01:05:52.316
Ha Na!

763
01:05:57.769 --> 01:06:00.053
See, judo is all about aura.

764
01:06:00.053 --> 01:06:03.196
Once you get a grip, you use your "you're dead meat" stare.

765
01:06:50.996 --> 01:06:55.746
Police have referred Mr. Yang, the suspect charged with attempted murder of actress Yoon,

766
01:06:55.746 --> 01:06:58.890
to prosecution this morning.

767
01:06:58.890 --> 01:07:03.008
The chilling truth uncovered about Korea's most well-known film director

768
01:07:03.008 --> 01:07:06.496
has plunged the nation into shock and chaos.

769
01:07:06.496 --> 01:07:08.626
Moreover, the investigation of the crime scene

770
01:07:08.626 --> 01:07:13.877
led to the discovery of the body of a John Doe with severely damaged fingerprints and teeth,

771
01:07:13.877 --> 01:07:16.141
signaling that the case is more than an attempt,

772
01:07:16.141 --> 01:07:20.125
and will be treated as a serial violent crime case.

773
01:07:20.125 --> 01:07:23.569
With past crimes being uncovered on top of the attempted murder,

774
01:07:23.569 --> 01:07:29.120
experts speculate that he will not be able to escape a heavy sentence.

775
01:07:29.120 --> 01:07:33.070
The prosecution will focus heavily on the deliberate nature of the crime

776
01:07:33.070 --> 01:07:38.080
and the defendant's tendency to reoffend in this trial.

777
01:07:50.502 --> 01:07:53.122
I've been wondering something.

778
01:07:53.122 --> 01:07:55.369
Can I ask you a question?

779
01:07:55.369 --> 01:07:56.981
What is it?

780
01:07:57.609 --> 01:07:59.193
Tae Kang...

781
01:07:59.193 --> 01:08:01.261
You mean Do Hoon oppa?

782
01:08:01.261 --> 01:08:03.322
"Oppa?"

783
01:08:03.322 --> 01:08:05.694
Calling everyone "oppa" all willy-nilly...

784
01:08:09.876 --> 01:08:12.970
The proposal...

785
01:08:13.942 --> 01:08:17.742
Did you... say yes?

786
01:08:17.742 --> 01:08:19.905
How do you know about this?

787
01:08:22.482 --> 01:08:23.974
Just...

788
01:08:50.116 --> 01:08:52.091
I saw that coming.

789
01:08:53.322 --> 01:08:56.173
But it still hurts to be rejected.

790
01:08:57.549 --> 01:08:59.402
I'm sorry.

791
01:08:59.402 --> 01:09:01.902
Your feelings are too valuable to get hurt like this.

792
01:09:04.942 --> 01:09:07.929
I was too late in realizing this, but...

793
01:09:07.929 --> 01:09:09.629
Yoon Ha Ru.

794
01:09:10.696 --> 01:09:13.223
He's not my past, but still my present.

795
01:09:15.889 --> 01:09:17.407
Then...

796
01:09:18.636 --> 01:09:20.023
What?

797
01:09:21.036 --> 01:09:25.446
That means I'm not your past, but your present.

798
01:09:25.446 --> 01:09:28.224
So I still have a chance...

799
01:09:28.224 --> 01:09:29.924
Right?

800
01:09:31.662 --> 01:09:35.273
What if... you do?

801
01:09:39.309 --> 01:09:42.054
It's hard to explain,

802
01:09:42.866 --> 01:09:45.796
but I can tell you one thing.

803
01:09:45.796 --> 01:09:48.085
Any time spent without you...

804
01:09:48.742 --> 01:09:50.893
has no meaning at all to me.

805
01:09:56.258 --> 01:09:58.606
You may not know,

806
01:09:59.496 --> 01:10:02.129
but my past has been Seo Ye Rang,

807
01:10:04.062 --> 01:10:07.613
and every bit of the present that I have left in the future,

808
01:10:07.613 --> 01:10:09.313
all of it,

809
01:10:10.082 --> 01:10:11.782
is you, Seo Ye Rang.

810
01:10:18.336 --> 01:10:20.236
Come back to me.

811
01:10:21.976 --> 01:10:24.306
I won't make you feel lonely.

812
01:10:24.306 --> 01:10:26.362
I won't keep you waiting.

813
01:10:26.982 --> 01:10:28.570
I promise...

814
01:10:29.176 --> 01:10:33.169
I'll be your boss... this time.

815
01:11:15.202 --> 01:11:17.229
It's been hard, hasn't it?

816
01:11:19.542 --> 01:11:21.515
I'm sorry.

817
01:11:21.515 --> 01:11:23.355
And thank you.

818
01:11:26.553 --> 01:11:28.816
I should've confessed first.

819
01:11:30.322 --> 01:11:32.826
I could've had all this happiness,

820
01:11:32.826 --> 01:11:35.724
but I was scared to tell you that I love you.

821
01:11:35.724 --> 01:11:37.625
All that needless struggling...

822
01:11:42.702 --> 01:11:44.213
I like you.

823
01:11:44.213 --> 01:11:45.557
Woo Jae.

824
01:11:45.557 --> 01:11:49.309
I like you so, so much.

825
01:11:51.809 --> 01:11:54.853
I love you, Ha Na.

826
01:11:54.853 --> 01:11:56.362
I love you more.

827
01:11:59.320 --> 01:12:02.284
No, I think my love is bigger.

828
01:12:02.284 --> 01:12:04.893
Alright. Whatever you say.

829
01:12:11.120 --> 01:12:14.898
You know what the most cruel part of it was?

830
01:12:16.967 --> 01:12:19.112
The moment I lost you...

831
01:12:20.247 --> 01:12:23.683
all the emotions that I had lost came flooding back.

832
01:12:25.314 --> 01:12:28.534
You always manage to save me, in whatever way.

833
01:12:30.527 --> 01:12:32.171
But now,

834
01:12:32.171 --> 01:12:34.091
you've saved me.

835
01:12:40.380 --> 01:12:42.951
I was crying so hard when you saved me.

836
01:12:42.951 --> 01:12:45.055
You know what you said?

837
01:12:45.774 --> 01:12:47.151
What?

838
01:12:47.151 --> 01:12:50.246
You saw me cry and said, "Thank goodness."

839
01:12:50.246 --> 01:12:51.677
Dummy.

840
01:12:54.207 --> 01:12:56.936
I may be a dummy, but I'm still happy.

841
01:12:58.174 --> 01:13:00.003
Don't hurt.

842
01:13:00.934 --> 01:13:02.634
And don't get hurt, either.

843
01:13:03.474 --> 01:13:05.174
Promise me.

844
01:13:07.527 --> 01:13:09.450
You promise me, too.

845
01:13:34.587 --> 01:13:37.093
The camcorder disappeared,

846
01:13:41.034 --> 01:13:46.265
and our summer that seemed unending had come to an end.

847
01:13:54.520 --> 01:13:57.392
There was no more time traveling,

848
01:13:58.032 --> 01:14:01.056
but we were together.

849
01:14:40.747 --> 01:14:44.940
Could everything have been a gift from god?

850
01:14:44.940 --> 01:14:51.431
As for why we were granted such miracles, it's still a mystery.

851
01:14:52.140 --> 01:14:54.051
But we came to the realization

852
01:14:54.051 --> 01:14:57.982
that our hands, intertwined, and this warmth...

853
01:14:57.982 --> 01:15:02.658
is the grandest magic of all, protecting each other.

854
01:15:04.374 --> 01:15:11.608
The Best Actress Award of the 31st Baekryong Film Awards, 2027,

855
01:15:13.794 --> 01:15:15.124
goes to...

856
01:15:15.124 --> 01:15:19.162
Yoon Ha Na, from "Every day with Yesterday's Miracle."

857
01:15:19.162 --> 01:15:21.289
Congratulations!

858
01:15:31.574 --> 01:15:35.225
Yoon Ha Na, as Yoon Mi Gyeong

859
01:15:35.225 --> 01:15:37.682
in Director Na's film, "Every day with Yesterday's Miracle,"

860
01:15:37.682 --> 01:15:41.113
had skillfully transformed human sadness into a dazzling sense of liveliness,

861
01:15:41.113 --> 01:15:44.701
receiving countless compliments about her astonishing proficiency.

862
01:15:44.701 --> 01:15:48.841
She had endured a long time acting in nameless, short-lived roles.

863
01:15:48.841 --> 01:15:53.852
The silent journey that she had taken, and her seemingly endless passion for acting

864
01:15:53.852 --> 01:15:58.884
make today's award an even more valuable one.

865
01:16:02.268 --> 01:16:04.174
Thank you so much.

866
01:16:05.428 --> 01:16:07.128
So this is...

867
01:16:09.488 --> 01:16:12.574
what it feels like.

868
01:16:14.994 --> 01:16:19.725
I'm thankful for the tears that I'm shedding,

869
01:16:19.725 --> 01:16:22.338
and I feel blessed tonight.

870
01:16:30.241 --> 01:16:35.049
I have always learned the world by living through my roles.

871
01:16:35.049 --> 01:16:37.306
That's how I grew.

872
01:16:37.965 --> 01:16:40.578
This role was no exception to that.

873
01:16:42.428 --> 01:16:45.021
Yoon Mi Gyeong and Yoon Ha Na...

874
01:16:45.821 --> 01:16:49.356
had a lot in common, luckily for me.

875
01:16:51.154 --> 01:16:54.412
They both had been broken

876
01:16:54.412 --> 01:17:00.016
from trying to ignore the emotions that would come crashing toward them.

877
01:17:01.901 --> 01:17:06.565
They both had failed to see the miracles that they already had,

878
01:17:07.314 --> 01:17:10.957
and had been fooled by the false concept of "a better future,"

879
01:17:11.594 --> 01:17:14.367
coveting an unattainable miracle.

880
01:17:15.461 --> 01:17:17.865
All that time spent,

881
01:17:17.865 --> 01:17:20.468
hurting not only others,

882
01:17:20.468 --> 01:17:23.704
but myself as well...

883
01:17:23.704 --> 01:17:29.008
Living Mi Gyeong's and my days,

884
01:17:29.691 --> 01:17:31.975
I finally opened my eyes.

885
01:17:31.975 --> 01:17:34.779
I'm living in a world where I wake up every day...

886
01:17:39.418 --> 01:17:42.705
to the breath of my loved one,

887
01:17:43.928 --> 01:17:46.464
and I'm allowed to share that moment.

888
01:17:47.168 --> 01:17:49.634
I can hold their hands,

889
01:17:50.261 --> 01:17:53.563
and talk about the little things in life.

890
01:17:55.454 --> 01:17:58.324
That bit of warmth, so easily taken for granted,

891
01:17:58.987 --> 01:18:03.605
is the miracle of your every day, happening so close by.

892
01:18:04.421 --> 01:18:05.901
Please,

893
01:18:05.901 --> 01:18:09.654
I hope for all of you to discover your miracle,

894
01:18:09.654 --> 01:18:12.092
and to love it wholeheartedly.

895
01:18:12.092 --> 01:18:15.329
We, having endured countless yesterdays,

896
01:18:15.329 --> 01:18:18.454
to finally meet our today,

897
01:18:18.454 --> 01:18:21.170
are already the glorious miracles.

898
01:18:21.898 --> 01:18:24.592
I hope you never forget that.

899
01:18:27.282 --> 01:18:29.179
Thank you.

900
01:18:57.588 --> 01:18:59.079
Ha Na.

901
01:18:59.668 --> 01:19:01.392
Yeah?

902
01:19:01.392 --> 01:19:03.988
What... do you dream of?

903
01:19:03.988 --> 01:19:05.761
My dream?

904
01:19:05.761 --> 01:19:07.334
That's sudden.

905
01:19:10.602 --> 01:19:12.748
All of them have already come true.

906
01:19:14.615 --> 01:19:18.285
I'm with you right now, aren't I?

907
01:19:20.595 --> 01:19:21.981
What about you?

908
01:19:25.675 --> 01:19:27.106
I don't know.

909
01:19:27.106 --> 01:19:29.230
What could I possibly dream of?

910
01:19:29.230 --> 01:19:30.714
I have no clue.

911
01:19:30.714 --> 01:19:33.220
What could you possibly dream of?

912
01:19:34.068 --> 01:19:37.341
What about after your dream comes true? What do you want to do then?

913
01:19:37.341 --> 01:19:41.407
What do you think you'd want to do the most?

914
01:19:42.675 --> 01:19:44.435
Ha Na.

915
01:19:44.435 --> 01:19:45.722
Yes?

916
01:20:18.915 --> 01:20:20.615
I dream of...

917
01:20:21.902 --> 01:20:23.375
you.

918
01:20:24.215 --> 01:20:25.718
Ha Na,

919
01:20:28.342 --> 01:20:30.042
will you...

920
01:20:31.122 --> 01:20:33.134
be mine, forever?

921
01:21:59.255 --> 01:22:01.014
Hey, kiddos.

922
01:22:01.014 --> 01:22:03.996
If you're ever lost, you can ask me.

923
01:22:05.742 --> 01:22:07.782
Ta-da!

924
01:22:08.842 --> 01:22:10.246
What?

925
01:22:13.575 --> 01:22:14.746
Babe?

926
01:22:14.746 --> 01:22:19.674
Ha Na's ring... is so big and pretty, don't you think?

927
01:22:20.755 --> 01:22:24.439
You know my love for you is bigger than some diamond!

928
01:22:24.439 --> 01:22:27.296
Then make up for it by making me breakfast every day for the rest of our lives.

929
01:22:27.296 --> 01:22:28.534
- Sure! - Really?

930
01:22:28.534 --> 01:22:30.091
Of course!

931
01:22:30.091 --> 01:22:31.988
So cute!

932
01:22:31.988 --> 01:22:33.386
Anyway, Woo Jae,

933
01:22:33.386 --> 01:22:36.436
are you sure you can handle her?

934
01:22:36.436 --> 01:22:38.136
Of course I can.

935
01:22:39.722 --> 01:22:42.307
Hey, both of you, cut it out!

936
01:22:42.307 --> 01:22:44.475
Stop it, I'm starving.

937
01:22:44.475 --> 01:22:46.341
- Let's get something to eat. - Really?

938
01:22:46.341 --> 01:22:47.670
You should pay.

939
01:23:04.748 --> 01:23:08.326
[If you have someone who, in your eyes, lights up the world,]

940
01:23:10.677 --> 01:23:14.719
[tell them how much you love them before it's too late.]

941
01:23:16.256 --> 01:23:19.736
[Your today is too bright to harbor any hesitation.]
